  "created_at": "2026-11-04T00:14:53Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-11-04T00:14:53Z",
  "body": ">  The 2-way binding guide does mention\n>  > Two way binding is a shorthand to simultaneously bind a value into an element, while also giving that element the ability to propagate changes back through this binding.\n> \n>  This should imho is enough to infer everything. Don't you agree?\n\nThe statements \"bind a value into an element\" and \"propagate changes back through this binding\" are vague, and do not convey the precise information described at the top of this ticket. It may be a decent one-sentence introduction into this topic, but it's not a sufficient explanation of the entire idea and its key details.\n\nI know plenty of people with years of Angular experience, who do not know these things. So I guess we, as the Angular community, are not doing enough to share this information. Putting it in the documentation would be a step in the right direction.",
